   "type": "text",
   "text": "✗ **H0110_L1_flat_beam_lns_cse_sieve** · hypothesis\n\nMulti-threaded C++ CSE reducer (clss_cse_beam_reducer.cpp) combining flat-array representation with Greedy-Potential (gp), Beam-Lookahead, partial LNS reinitialization (destroy-and-repair of fresh variables), and scanning alternative ZT schemes from Perminov's repository will beat cr records on >= 3 formats with max(n,m,p) <= 8 (full win + p3).\n\n*why dead:* [L-FACR-001=0] Purely syntactic CSE (disjoint subsets without algebraic cancellation) stalls at cr=391 on 4x5x6 (vs 380 in ternary_addition_reducer and 345 in the 2026-10-19 files), because the record files from commit 048b64987b exploit algebraic cancellation (fresh_cancellations=10,16,5 and el_cancellations=9,11,11 in the fresh-variable DAG).",
   "x": 0,
   "y": 0,
